# Blender's own rolling backups -- written on every save, never wanted.
*.blend1
*.blend2
__pycache__/

# Preview renders. Every one of these is reproducible by re-running the script
# beside it, and they are the largest thing in this folder by a distance --
# the first clean-up here removed 25.5 MB of superseded previews against 8.9 MB
# of everything else. What IS worth committing is in `skins/`: those are the
# textures that get uploaded, so they are the source of a shipped asset rather
# than a picture of one.
*.png
!**/skins/**/*.png

# `renders/` is where every preview script writes now, so a session of looking
# at the pig cannot bury the .obj files that ship. Covered by the rule above
# already; named here so the folder reads as deliberate rather than as debris.
renders/

# THE MASKS UNDER `skins/` ARE THE ONE THING HERE THAT CANNOT BE REGENERATED.
# Everything else in this folder is output: the .obj files come from
# `build_pig.py`, the previews from the script beside them, the procedural maps
# from `make_animal_maps.py`. A hand-painted greyscale mask has no generator, so
# losing one is losing the work rather than a re-run. They are inside `skins/`
# specifically so the un-ignore above keeps them.

# The scene files are large and are rebuilt by `build_pig.py` and
# `make_fur_tufts.py` from source that IS committed. The .obj exports are the
# things actually uploaded to Roblox, so they stay.
*.blend

# ---- what is regenerable, measured rather than assumed --------------------
#
# The policy above keeps `skins/**/*.png` and the .obj exports on the grounds
# that they are the source of a shipped asset. That is right about WHICH files
# matter and wrong about which of them git has to carry: measured, the .obj
# exports are 8.3 MB and the colour maps 14.5 MB, and every one of them is
# written by a script committed beside it -- build_pig.py for the meshes,
# bake_skin.py and make_animal_maps.py for the maps. Re-running a script is
# cheap; carrying 23 MB in every clone forever is not.
#
# THE ALPHA MASKS STAY, and they are the whole reason this is a rule rather
# than a blanket ignore. The note above is correct that a hand-painted mask
# has no generator, so losing one is losing the work. They are 1.5 MB.
*_color.png
*_alpha.png
!**/skins/**/*_alpha.png
*.obj

# Raw third-party downloads. The Meshy AI export is 12.8 MB of texture and
# FBX that was an INPUT to the stormwolf bake -- it is re-downloadable, it is
# somebody else's output, and nothing in the pipeline reads it after the bake.
**/source/
